From: Tao Gong <gongtao0607@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: flowtable: skip the bridge VLAN push for VLAN device ports

When a bridge port is a VLAN device (e.g. lan2.21), the path walk sets it
as the transmit device and also records its VLAN as encap. The bridge fast
path then pushes that VLAN and transmits through the VLAN device, which
adds the same tag again. The frame leaves double tagged and is lost. TCP
connections establish and then stall, as the handshake still takes the
slow path.

Do not push the tag when the transmit device differs from the hardware
device, i.e. when a VLAN device adds it.

Signed-off-by: Tao Gong <gongtao0607@gmail.com>
---
--- a/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_ip.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_ip.c
@@ -376,6 +376,7 @@ static void nf_flow_bridge_vlan_push(str
 				     struct sk_buff *skb)
 {
 	const struct flow_offload_tuple *other = &flow->tuplehash[!dir].tuple;
+	const struct flow_offload_tuple *this = &flow->tuplehash[dir].tuple;
 
 	if (flow_table->type->family != NFPROTO_BRIDGE || !other->encap_num)
 		return;
@@ -384,6 +385,10 @@ static void nf_flow_bridge_vlan_push(str
 	if (other->in_vlan_ingress & BIT(0))
 		return;
 
+	/* Egress port is a VLAN device, which adds its tag itself */
+	if (this->out.ifidx != this->out.hw_ifidx)
+		return;
+
 	if (other->encap[0].proto == htons(ETH_P_8021Q) ||
 	    other->encap[0].proto == htons(ETH_P_8021AD))
 		__vlan_hwaccel_put_tag(skb, other->encap[0].proto,
